# Line endings.
#
# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository and check it out with the
# platform's native endings. The baseline commit already stores LF for all text
# files (verified with `git ls-files --eol`: every entry is i/lf, and the four
# PNGs are i/-text), so this records the state the repo is already in -- it does
# not renormalize anything. What it DOES do is make that state independent of
# each contributor's core.autocrlf setting, which is what produced the
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings on a machine with autocrlf=true.
* text=auto

# Binary assets -- never normalize, never diff as text.
# extension/icons/*.png are generated by tools/make_icons.py.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.zip  binary
*.whl  binary

# Platform-specific scripts need the endings their interpreter expects no
# matter who checked them out: a .sh with CRLF dies with "\r: command not
# found", and some Windows tooling still chokes on a .bat with bare LF.
# None are tracked today; these rules are here so the first one added is right.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.sh  text eol=lf
